
---
import AnimeFinder from "../components/AnimeFinder.astro";

const title = "Find Anime | Bezels";
const description =
  "Discover anime based on your favourite genres, moods and story preferences with the Bezels Anime Finder.";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <style>
      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
      }

      body {
        background: #090d18;
        color: #f4f6ff;
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        min-height: 100vh;
      }

      header {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: center;
        padding: 22px 8%;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #20283b;
      }

      .logo {
        font-size: 27px;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: white;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .logo span {
        color: #8b7cff;
      }

      nav {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 22px;
      }

      nav a {
        color: #b9bfd1;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-size: 14px;
      }

      nav a:hover,
      nav a.active {
        color: #a99aff;
      }

      .page-intro {
        max-width: 850px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 75px 22px 35px;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        color: #a99aff;
        font-size: 12px;
        letter-spacing: 2px;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 55px);
        margin: 18px 0;
      }

      h1 span {
        color: #9685ff;
      }

      .page-intro p {
        color: #aab2c6;
        line-height: 1.8;
        font-size: 16px;
      }

      .article {
        max-width: 850px;
        margin: 60px auto;
        padding: 0 22px;
        color: #c5ccdc;
        line-height: 1.9;
      }

      .article h2 {
        color: white;
        font-size: 25px;
        margin: 35px 0 12px;
      }

      .article h3 {
        color: #e6e2ff;
        font-size: 19px;
        margin: 25px 0 10px;
      }

      .article p {
        margin-bottom: 16px;
      }

      .article ul {
        padding-left: 24px;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
      }

      footer {
        text-align: center;
        border-top: 1px solid #20283b;
        padding: 28px;
        color: #828da5;
        font-size: 13px;
      }

      @media (max-width: 650px) {
        header {
          padding: 20px;
          flex-direction: column;
          gap: 18px;
        }

        nav {
          justify-content: center;
          gap: 14px;
        }

        nav a {
          font-size: 12px;
        }

        .page-intro {
          padding-top: 55px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header>
      <a class="logo" href="/">BEZELS<span>.</span></a>
      <nav>
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/find-anime/" class="active">Find Anime</a>
        <a href="/anime-quiz/">Anime Quiz</a>
        <a href="/watchlist/">My Watchlist</a>
        <a href="/articles/">Articles</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="page-intro">
        <span class="eyebrow">BEZELS ANIME FINDER</span>
        <h1>Find Your Next <span>Anime.</span></h1>
        <p>
          Not sure what to watch next? Use our anime finder to explore
          recommendations based on genres, moods, episode counts and story
          preferences.
        </p>
      </section>

      <AnimeFinder />

      <article class="article">
        <h2>How to Find Anime That Matches Your Interests</h2>

        <p>
          Choosing a new anime can be difficult, especially when there are
          hundreds of different shows available. Some viewers enjoy action
          and adventure, while others prefer emotional stories, mystery,
          comedy or fantasy.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Bezels Anime Finder helps make that decision easier by letting
          you explore anime using preferences that matter to you. Instead of
          browsing random titles, you can narrow down your choices and
          discover shows that match your interests.
        </p>

        <h2>Choose Your Favourite Genres</h2>

        <p>
          Genres are a useful starting point when searching for anime.
          Action, romance, fantasy, thriller, comedy and science fiction
          offer very different viewing experiences. Selecting genres you
          enjoy helps the finder identify more relevant recommendations.
        </p>

        <h2>Find Anime Based on Your Mood</h2>

        <p>
          Your mood can influence what kind of story you want to watch.
          Sometimes you may want something exciting and adventurous.
          At other times, a relaxing comedy or an emotional drama might
          be a better choice.
        </p>

        <h2>Consider the Episode Count</h2>

        <p>
          The length of an anime series is another important factor.
          Shorter shows can be convenient when you have limited time,
          while longer series offer more room for extended stories
          and character development.
        </p>

        <h2>Explore Stories Beyond Popular Titles</h2>

        <p>
          Popular anime are not the only shows worth watching. Exploring
          different genres, storytelling styles and types of protagonists
          can help you discover series you might otherwise overlook.
          Try different preferences and use the recommendations as a
          starting point for your next watch.
        </p>

        <h2>Start Discovering Anime</h2>

        <p>
          Use the Bezels Anime Finder above to explore titles that fit
          your preferences. You can experiment with different filters
          whenever you want to discover something new.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>

    <footer>© 2026 Bezels. Made for anime fans.</footer>
  </body>
</html>
